  "id": "Compound::DB01181 - Gene::1548",
  "verbalization": "Ifosfamide is linked to Cyp2a6 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the cytochrome P450 family, specifically Cyp2a6. The evidence suggests that Ifosfamide binds to Cyp2c18 and Cyp2b6, which are both involved in the metabolism of arachidonic acid, a key precursor in the production of pro-inflammatory lipid mediators. This binding may trigger a cascade of enzymatic activities that ultimately lead to the participation of Cyp2a6 in the same metabolic pathway. Additionally, the evidence indicates that Ifosfamide can cause myocardial hemorrhage, which is associated with Cyclophosphamide, a compound that binds to Cyp2a6. This suggests that the interaction between Ifosfamide and Cyp2a6 may be mediated through shared metabolic pathways or enzymatic activities, potentially involving the same cytochrome P450 enzymes. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Ifosfamide influences Cyp2a6, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
